[Music]  when the villain in a movie is nicknamed  the god butcher it's safe to assume that  not everyone is going to make it out  alive so who gets it in thor love and  thunder keep watching to find out  oh god we're going to die  taika ytt is a master at blending absurd  comedy with emotional storytelling  especially when it comes to kids and  their parental figures thor love and  thunder eventually fits that mold but it  starts off on a note that's completely  humorless unexpectedly dark and almost  too tragic to be believed in what was  advertised as a zany mcu movie gore and  his daughter whose name we don't know  are seeking shelter from destructive  sandstorms and looking for even so much  as a drop of water despite gore's  prayers their planet has become  uninhabitable and their civilization has  been lost the girl doodles on rocks  while gore prays to his god rapu some  time passes we don't know how much and  gore holds his child in his arms as  she's dying of thirst she tells him that  she's tired before she passes away in  front of his eyes he buries her on his  home planet and decorates her grave with  rocks though the audience surely went in  anticipating that they'd be rooting  against gore the scene is played with  such devastating realism you can't help  but mourn for the little girl and  sympathize with her father who becomes  the god butcher because of this seismic  loss oh god she will die  it's a sad irony that gore spots an  oasis only after his dear daughter's  death as he stumbles over to the  tree-lined watering hole he can't quite  tell if what lies before him is real or  an illusion he collapses into the water  then notices something rustling behind  all the greenery it's rapu played by  ytt's what we do in the shadow's co-star  jonathan bruff the god to whom gore had  been praying decked out in gold with an  ostentatious headpiece gore assumes rapu  is welcoming him into the afterlife he  shows rapu the pendant he wears around  his neck to mark himself as one of his  followers but rapu isn't there to save  anybody he's chilling with the flower  gods and has long been entirely  indifferent to gore's people's suffering  rapu's main concern is the existence of  the necrosaur a weapon that can kill  gods at a price and that conveniently  now rests near gore's right hand when  gore tells rapu that his kingdom is  fallen the god shrugs it off and says  there will always be new souls to  worship him he breaks the bad news to  his last remaining devotee there is no  eternal reward that enrages an already  spiritually broken gore who rips the  religious pendant from his neck and is  suddenly able to wield the levitating  necrosword he uses it to stab a taken  aback rapoo in the throat and it's  implied he decapitates him to finish the  job  after he becomes aware of gore the god  butcher thor discovers distressed  signals from all across the universe in  one he sees lady sith gravely injured  thor and korg make haste to try and  rescue his fellow asgardian warrior but  when they arrive they're not so  pleasantly greeted by the mountain-sized  corpse of a frost-covered creature korg  asks who or what it is and he clearly  shaken thor replies that this is falagar  one of the nicest gods anybody could  ever hope to meet valagar appeared in  the promotional material for thor love  and thunder and it intrigued comic book  fans as it's a pretty precise recreation  of a panel from thor god of thunder  volume one number three though the film  doesn't get into much detail about  falliger or his relationship with thor  at all both use him in much the same way  on the page falagar is an old friend of  thor's who rules over the galactic  frontier and enjoys sparring even  against black holes after some years  apart from each other thor learns that  falagar is dead at the hands of gore the  godbutcher thor's line to korg suggests  they had a similar friendship in the mcu  and here too he meets his end because of  gore's vow to wipe out all the gods  though his enormous lifeless body makes  for a breathtaking shot it's a shame we  didn't get to see this peculiar majestic  god in action  thor and mighty thor team up to  successfully destroy the necrosword but  they don't do it quick enough to stop  gore the godbutcher from using  stormbreaker to open the gate to  eternity as gore walks through the  circular door into eternity's realm and  stands before the powerful living cosmic  entity represented as a galactic  silhouette thor tells him that he's one  meanwhile jane who used her last ounce  of strength as mighty thor to wield  mjolnir against the necrosword falls to  the watery ground as a cancer patient  once again she and thor have a final  conversation that moves him and changes  his plan gore comes to realize that with  his one wish to eternity he could bring  back his daughter rather than  exterminate the gods however the necro  sword corrupted his own body so much he  knows that like jane he's about to die  too even though he won't be around to  see the ramifications of his choice he  decides to give his daughter another  chance at life rather than fulfill his  vow of vengeance jane promises that she  won't be alone and gore lives just long  enough to say goodbye to his resurrected  child and to ask thor to promise to  protect her in the scene that follows we  see thor has adopted her and is raising  her to be an asgardian warrior like him  and that gore redeemed himself in thor's  eyes by choosing love instead of hate  early on in thor love and thunder we  learn that jane's been diagnosed with  stage four cancer and it isn't  responding to treatment while in her  office she flips through an old book of  norse mythology and notices the word  mjolnir feeling called to her former  boyfriend's former weapon she travels to  new asgard incognito and tries to summon  the hammer we learn from a montage of  their relationship that thor once  ordered mjolnir to protect jane his true  love this produced powerful magic that  bound the hammer to jane and for a while  jane in the audience think that magic is  healing her as it gives her superhuman  strength let's bring the rainbow but  when she lands back in the hospital  worse for the wear every time she suits  up as mighty thor she figures out what's  really going on mjolnir is actually  using up her remaining life force once  jane comes clean to thor about her  condition he begs her not to pick up the  hammer again and tells her that he loves  her he hopes that they can find a cure  and still have a chance at a life  together once he returns from facing  gore alone jane understands his request  but she knows there's likely no cure she  joins her love for one last classic thor  adventure and with her dying breaths  tells him that she's content that she  lived an extraordinary albeit short life  for a human they end their relationship  on sad but good terms as she vanishes  the end credits scene reveals that since  she died of viking on the battlefield  she's welcomed into valhalla by none  other than heimdall  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  thor love and thunder are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

